md:253:**AC-3.1:** During process stages that support discussion or clarification, the\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:266:**AC-3.2:** When the process is waiting on a specific question, decision, or\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:274:- **TC-3.2b: Outstanding request clears or changes after response**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:277:  - Then: The outstanding request clears or is replaced by the new current request\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:279:**AC-3.3:** A submitted user response becomes part of durable process history\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:282:- **TC-3.3a: Submitted response appears in process history**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:283:  - Given: User submits a response in a process work surface\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:285:  - Then: The response appears in that process's visible history\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:287:  - Given: User previously submitted a response in a process\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:289:  - Then: The response still appears in that process's visible history\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:291:**AC-3.4:** When the current process state does not accept a user response, the\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:304:**AC-3.5:** An invalid process response is rejected without creating a new\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:307:- **TC-3.5a: Empty response is rejected**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:308:  - Given: User is in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:309:  - When: User submits an empty or invalid response\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:310:  - Then: The response is rejected and no new visible history item is created\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:311:- **TC-3.5b: Failed response submission does not create partial history**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:312:  - Given: User submits a response in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:316:**AC-3.6:** After a successful process response submission, the submitted\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:317:response and resulting process state update appear in the same session without\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:320:- **TC-3.6a: Successful response appears in visible history in same session**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:321:  - Given: User submits a valid response in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:323:  - Then: The submitted response appears in visible history in the same session without requiring manual refresh\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:324:- **TC-3.6b: Resulting current request or process state updates in same session**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:325:  - Given: User submits a valid response in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:417:- **TC-5.1a: Routine progress remains distinct from attention-required request**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:421:- **TC-5.1b: Attention-required item remains visible in mixed activity**\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:422:  - Given: Process continues to report routine progress around a current request\\\\\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/e