process-environment.service.ts:1111:        archiveEntries: args.deferredArchiveEntries,\ndocs/setup/local-bootstrap.md:25:- `pnpm verify-all`\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:375:Every project needs at least four verification tiers: `red-verify` (everything except tests — for TDD Red exit when stubs throw), `verify` (standard development gate), `green-verify` (verify + test immutability guard — for TDD Green exit), and `verify-all` (deep verification including integration and e2e suites). Define the specific commands for each tier in the tech design so stories can reference them consistently.\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2438:| `green-verify` | Quality gate for TDD Green exit | After implementation passes tests | `verify` + test-immutability guard |\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2439:| `verify-all` | Deep verification for integration and release | Story completion, pre-release | `verify` + integration + e2e suites |\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2443:`green-verify` exists because Red tests are the behavioral contract for Green. Test files should not be modified during Green implementation. `green-verify` runs the standard verification pipeline then checks that no test files were changed.\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2445:If integration or e2e suites don't exist yet, `verify-all` should still exist as a wirable command from day one. The placeholder should output a clear notice that the suite isn't implemented yet (e.g., \"SKIP: integration suite not yet implemented\") and exit successfully so CI doesn't break — but never silently pass as if verification occurred.\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2454:    \"green-verify\": \"bun run verify && bun run guard:no-test-changes\",\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2455:    \"verify-all\": \"bun run verify && bun run test:integration && bun run test:e2e\"\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2460:The specific commands vary by stack. The principle is consistent: `red-verify` = everything except tests, `verify` = standard gate, `green-verify` = verify + test immutability, `verify-all` = verify + deep suites.\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2529:**Exit Criteria:** `green-verify` passes (all tests PASS + no test files modified). Manual verification for this chunk complete.\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-tech-design/SKILL.md:2593:- [ ] Verification scripts defined (`red-verify`, `verify`, `green-verify`, `verify-all`) with specific command composition\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:7:import { DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.js';\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:8:import { DefaultTurnDerivationService } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.js';\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:68:  archiveEntries: ArchiveEntry[] = readyArchivePageFixture.entries,\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:83:    archiveEntriesByProcessId: {\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:84:      [processId]: archiveEntries,\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:90:  archiveEntries: ArchiveEntry[] = readyArchivePageFixture.entries,\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:92:  archiveEntries: ArchiveEntry[];\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:95:  const store = buildServiceStore(archiveEntries);\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:96:  const turnDerivationService = new DefaultTurnDerivationService(store, {\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:101:  const derivedArchiveViewService = new DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService(\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:121:    archiveEntries: archivePage.entries,\ntests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:210:    expect(response.archiveEntries).toEqual(\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:21:  finalizationKey: 'response:history-user-001',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:41:  finalizationKey: 'model:message-001',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:61:  finalizationKey: 'reasoning:001',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:81:  finalizationKey: 'script:001',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:101:  finalizationKey: 'tool:lint:call',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:123:  finalizationKey: 'tool:lint:result',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:145:  finalizationKey: 'event:completed',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:165:  finalizationKey: 'event:degraded',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:248:  viewKind: 'turn_range',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:268:  viewKind: 'chunk_candidate',\ntests/fixtures/archive.ts:288:  viewKind: 'chunk_candidate',\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-team-impl-cc/SKILL.md:223:1. Review the TDD_EVIDENCE: all tests passing, any test files modified during green and why, green-verify gate status.\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-team-impl-cc/SKILL.md:493:- Verification gates (red-verify, green-verify, story, and epic)\nreferences/full-liminal-spec-skills/ls-team-impl-cc/SKILL.md:684:  5. Run the project's green-verify gate (verify + test immutability).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/test-plan.md:24:| `green-verify` | `pnpm verify && pnpm guard:no-test-changes` | Green exit gate |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/test-plan.md:25:| `verify-all` | `pnpm verify && pnpm test:integration && pnpm test:e2e` | Deep verification; suites may initially emit `SKIP:` and pass |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/test-plan.md:45:Planned but not required for the first TDD cycles. `verify-all` should already\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design-server.md:730:environment, but that is a `verify-all` concern, not the primary TDD layer.