rtifacts/02-manage-purpose-access-mode-and-target-ref/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:946:epicGate: \"corepack pnpm run verify-all\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"725b0526-6c15-4d1c-bfda-b06961165f11\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df43c-e0a0-7302-a4ed-61ebb6077974\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df43c-e0a0-7302-a4ed-61ebb6077974\",\"storyId\":\"01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Attach Repositories to a Project or Process\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/003-implementor.json\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/routes/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/schemas/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-management.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-identity.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/github-repository-resolver.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 1 against the story AC/TCs and Flow 1 design, tracing the attach path from Fastify routes through source-management orchestration, Convex persistence/current-source mutation, and the project/process client surfaces. I also ran the mapped focused tests plus the story and epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project and process attach flows are still API-only because no UI action was implemented on either required surface\",\"evidence\":\"The story scope explicitly includes a project-scoped attach UI action and a process-scoped attach UI action, and AC-1.1 expects the user to attach while viewing the project shell or process work surface (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:24-25,49-58). The project shell still renders only the existing Create process button plus passive sections (apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts:71-99), the source attachment section is read-only markup with no form/button/callback (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts:24-69), and the process work surface only renders existing controls/materials/history/side-work with no attach affordance or handler (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:183-221). No client module calls the new POST /api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments or /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments routes, so a user cannot complete TC-1.1a or TC-1.1b from the required UI surfaces.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-02\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Process-scoped attaches cannot show repository identity and scope on the process surface immediately after creation\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.2 requires the new attachment's repository identity and chosen scope to be visible immediately after creation (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29-30,60-65). The process-surface contract cannot carry that data: ProcessSourceReference omits repositoryFullName and attachmentScope (apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:318-330), the materials reader only projects displayName/purpose/accessMode/repositoryUrl/targetRef/hydrationState/updatedAt into currentSources (apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:90-99), and the process materials UI renders purpose/access/hydration/target ref/updated only (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:220-253). The process attach API test likewise asserts only displayName and targetRef in materials.currentSources (tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:223-234), while the lone TC-1.2 client test only covers the project shell source section (tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts:13-31).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.2\",\"TC-1.2a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project and process attach flows are still API-only because no UI action was implemented on either required surface\",\"evidence\":\"The story scope explicitly includes a project-scoped attach UI action and a process-scoped attach UI action, and AC-1.1 expects the user to attach while viewing the project shell or process work surface (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:24-25,49-58). The project shell still renders only the existing Create process button plus passive sections (apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts:71-99), the source attachment section is read-only markup with no form/button/callback (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts:24-69), and the process work surface only renders existing controls/materials/history/side-work with no attach affordance or handler (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:183-221). No client module calls the new POST /api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments or /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments routes, so a user cannot complete TC-1.1a or TC-1.1b from the required UI surfaces.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-02\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Process-scoped attaches cannot show repository identity and scope on the process surface immediately after creation\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.2 requires the new attachment's repository identity and chosen scope to be visible immediately after creation (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29-30,60-65). The process-surface contract cannot carry that data: ProcessSourceReference omits repositoryFullName and attachmentScope (apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:318-330), the materials reader only projects displayName/purpose/accessMode/repositoryUrl/targetRef/hydrationState/updatedAt into currentSources (apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:90-99), and the process materials UI renders purpose/access/hydration/target ref/updated only (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:220-253). The process attach API test likewise asserts only displayName and targetRef in materials.currentSources (tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:223-234), while the lone TC-1.2 client test only covers the project shell source section (tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts:13-31).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.2\",\"TC-1.2a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.3a\",\"TC-1.3b\",\"TC-1.3c\",\"TC-1.4a\",\"TC-1.4b\"],\"u