\t| TC-4.3a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-4.3a archive unchanged after turn derivation` | Entry rows unchanged after rebuild |\\\\n    71\\\\t| TC-4.4a | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.4a degraded turn returned` | One degraded turn does not hide others |\\\\n    72\\\\t| TC-5.1a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.1a derived view returned for turn range` | `turn_range` view returned without summary text |\\\\n    73\\\\t| TC-5.2a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.2a derived view identifies boundary` | start/end turn indexes and entry refs |\\\\n    74\\\\t| TC-5.3a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.3a derived view references source turns` | Source turn ids present |\\\\n    75\\\\t| TC-5.3b | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.3b derived view can trace to archive entries` | Source archive ids present |\\\\n    76\\\\t| TC-5.4a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-5.4a archive remains after derived view creation` | Archive rows still readable |\\\\n    77\\\\t| TC-5.5a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-5.5a derived view failure leaves archive readable` | Archive read succeeds after failed refresh |\\\\n    78\\\\t| TC-5.5b | `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | `TC-5.5b derived view reports degraded status` | Client renders degraded view |\\\\n    79\\\\t| TC-6.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.1a artifact provenance visible from archive entry` | Artifact version context visible |\\\\n    80\\\\t| TC-6.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.2a source provenance visible from archive entry` | Repository identity/ref visible |\\\\n    81\\\\t| TC-6.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.3a missing source context degrades one entry` | Entry visible with degraded source context |\\\\n    82\\\\t| TC-6.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.3b missing artifact context degrades one entry` | Entry visible with degraded artifact context |\\\\n    83\\\\t| TC-7.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-7.1a archive and turn reads restore after reload` | Durable archive and cached/rebuilt turns readable |\\\\n    84\\\\t| TC-7.1b | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-7.1b derived view restores after reload` | View readable or rebuilt |\\\\n    85\\\\t| TC-7.2a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-7.2a canonical archive remains visible during derived-view failure` | Archive unaffected by view failure |\\\\n    86\\\\t| TC-7.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-7.3a archive read returns bounded page` | Page has limit and next cursor |\\\\n    87\\\\t\\\\n    88\\\\t## Non-TC Decided Tests\\\\n    89\\\\t\\\\n    90\\\\t| Test File | Test Description | Reason |\\\\n    91\\\\t|-----------|------------------|--------|\\\\n    92\\\\t| `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | archive contract schemas accept all Epic 7 entry kinds and reject non-finalized entries | Protects shared contract vocabulary before route work |\\\\n    93\\\\t| `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` | live history upserts still update current process history without creating archive rows | Protects live/archive separation |\\\\n    94\\\\t| `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` maps `process_message` to `model_message` only for finalized compatible items | Compatibility bridge clarity |\\\\n    95\\\\t| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | same `processId + finalizationKey` returns or no-ops existing archive row | Primitive idempotency guard below Story 2 service proofs |\\\\n    96\\\\t| `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | pre-user-message entries form deterministic turn zero | Edge case in grouping rules |\\\\n    97\\\\t| `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | turn-cache rebuild preserves stable turn provenance for derived views | Prevents dangling view references after rebuild |\\\\n    98\\\\t| `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `chunk_candidate` rejects generated summary body content | Prevents summarization scope creep |\\\\n    99\\\\t| `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | stale derived views are rebuilt from current turns without breaking archive reads | Covers rebuild consistency after new archive entries |\\\\n   100\\\\t| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | sequence assignment is atomic across same-process appends | Protects ordering under concurrent writes |\\\\n   101\\\\t| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | derived-view refresh conflict returns `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Error contract coverage |\\\\n   102\\\\t| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | invalid archive query returns `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Error contract coverage |\\\\n   103\\\\t\\\\n   104\\\\t## Chunk Test Counts\\\\n   105\\\\t\\\\n   106\\\\t| Chunk | TC Tests | Non-TC Tests | Total | Primary Files |\\\\n   107\\\\t|-------|----------|--------------|-------|---------------|\\\\n   108\\\\t| 0 Foundation | 0 | 1 | 1 | contract/schema/fixture tests |\\\\n   109\\\\t| 1 Archive persistence | 9 | 2 | 11 | Convex archive entries |\\\\n   110\\\\t| 2 Finalization boundary | 5 | 2 | 7 | archive finalization, live tests |\\\\n   111\\\\t| 3 Archive read/reopen | 7 | 1 | 8 | archive API, client archive section |\\\\n   112\\\\t| 4 Turn derivation | 5 | 2 | 7 | turn derivation service |\\\\n   113\\\\t| 5 Structural views | 7 | 3 | 10 | derived-view service/client |\\\\n   114\\\\t| 6 Provenance coherence | 4 | 0 | 4 | archive API enrichment |\\\\n   115\\\\t| 7 Reopen/bounded reads | 4 | 0 | 4 | archive API, derived-view service |\\\\n   116\\\\t| **Total** | **41** | **11** | **52** |  |\\\\n   117\\\\t\\\\n   118\\\\tEpic 7 has 41 named TCs. Non-TC tests cover live/archive separation,\\\\n   119\\\\tcompatibility mapping, turn-zero grouping, turn-cache rebuild stability,\\\\n   120\\\\tno-summary enforcement, stale/rebuilt derived views, primitive idempotency, atomic sequence\\\\n   121\\\\tassignment, invalid archive requests, and refresh conflict behavior.\\\\n   122\\\\t\\\\n   123\\\\t## Verification Gates\\\\n   124\\\\t\\\\n   125\\\\t| Phase | Command | Expected Result |\\\\n   126\\\\t|-------|---------|-----------------|\\\\n   127\\\\t| Skeleton / Red exit | `pnpm run red-verify` | Format, lint, typecheck, and build pass while new behavior tests fail against stubs |\\\\n   128\\\\t| Development | `pnpm run verify` | Standard project verification passes |\\\\n   129\\\\t| Green exit | `pnpm run green-verify` | All tests pass and no-test-change guard runs |\\\\n   130\\\\t| Story/Epic completion | `pnpm run verify-all` | Full verification, integration, and e2e scaffold pass |\\\\n   131\\\\t\\\\n   132\\\\t## Manual Verification Checklist\\\\n   133\\\\t\\\\n   134\\\\t1. Start Convex with `pnpm run convex:dev`.\\\\n   135\\\\t2. Start app server with `pnpm dev`.\\\\n   136\\\\t3. Run or simulate a process that finalizes user, model, tool, and process-event entries.\\\\n   137\\\\t4. Open the process archive surface and verify finalized entries are visible in order.\\\\n   138\\\\t5. Reload the process and verify archive entries remain visible without environment state.\\\\n   139\\\\t6. Open the turn view and verify turns reference source archive entries.\\\\n   140\\\\t7. Open derived views and verify structural turn ranges/chunk candidates have no generated summary text.\\\\n   141\\\\t8. Simulate missing related source/artifact context and verify only affected entries degrade.\\\\n   142\\\\t9. Verify archive reads return a bounded page with a next cursor.\\\\n   143\\\\t\\\\n   144\\\\t## Reconciliation\\\\n   145\\\\t\\\\n   146\\\\t- TC tests: 41\\\\n   147\\\\t- Non-TC decided tests: 11\\\\n   148\\\\t- Planned automated tests: 52\\