{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '612,640p'\"","aggregated_output":"   612\tsemantics are added in Flow 6. Read-time degradation must not mutate the\n   613\tcanonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\n   614\tas degraded.\n   615\t\n   616\t### Flow 4: Derive Turns\n   617\t\n   618\tThis flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\n   619\tin ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\n   620\twhen refresh/rebuild is requested.\n   621\t\n   622\tGrouping rules:\n   623\t\n   624\t1. `user_message` starts a new turn.\n   625\t2. Entries before the first user message form turn `0` if they exist.\n   626\t3. `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`,\n   627\t   `tool_result`, and `process_event` attach to the active turn.\n   628\t  4. A `tool_result` with `relatedToolCallId` stays in the same turn as its\n   629\t   matching `tool_call` when both are present.\n   630\t  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\n   631\t\n   632\tRebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\n   633\tor explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\n   634\tstable `turnId` and `turnIndex`.\n   635\t\n   636\t### Flow 5: Produce Minimal Structural Views\n   637\t\n   638\tThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.5. Structural views are generated from\n   639\tturns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\n   640\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
