{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md | sed -n '332,380p'\"","aggregated_output":"   332\t#### Acceptance Criteria\n   333\t\n   334\t**AC-5.1:** The platform can expose a non-summarizing structural derived view\n   335\tover one or more turns.\n   336\t\n   337\t- **TC-5.1a: Derived view returned for turn range**\n   338\t  - Given: A process has derived turns\n   339\t  - When: User requests a derived view\n   340\t  - Then: The platform returns a derived view that identifies the turn boundary\n   341\t    and does not require generated summary text\n   342\t\n   343\t**AC-5.2:** Derived views identify structural boundaries for the turns they\n   344\tcover.\n   345\t\n   346\t- **TC-5.2a: Derived view identifies boundary**\n   347\t  - Given: A derived view is returned for a turn range\n   348\t  - When: User or process inspects the view metadata\n   349\t  - Then: The view identifies its source turn range and covered archive-entry\n   350\t    references\n   351\t\n   352\t**AC-5.3:** Derived views preserve provenance back to turns and archive entries.\n   353\t\n   354\t- **TC-5.3a: Derived view references source turns**\n   355\t  - Given: A derived view is returned\n   356\t  - When: User inspects the view metadata\n   357\t  - Then: The view identifies the turn or turns it was derived from\n   358\t- **TC-5.3b: Derived view can trace to archive entries**\n   359\t  - Given: A derived view references turns\n   360\t  - When: The source archive references are inspected\n   361\t  - Then: The underlying archive entry references remain available\n   362\t\n   363\t**AC-5.4:** Derived views do not replace or delete full-fidelity archive entries.\n   364\t\n   365\t- **TC-5.4a: Archive remains after derived view creation**\n   366\t  - Given: A derived view has been created or refreshed\n   367\t  - When: User reads the canonical archive\n   368\t  - Then: The full-fidelity archive entries remain available\n   369\t\n   370\t**AC-5.5:** Derived-view generation can degrade without corrupting canonical archive state.\n   371\t\n   372\t- **TC-5.5a: Derived view failure leaves archive readable**\n   373\t  - Given: Derived-view generation fails\n   374\t  - When: User reads the canonical archive\n   375\t  - Then: The archive remains readable and unchanged\n   376\t- **TC-5.5b: Derived view reports degraded status**\n   377\t  - Given: A derived view cannot fully resolve source turns or metadata\n   378\t  - When: User reads the derived-view surface\n   379\t  - Then: The platform returns a degraded derived-view state without hiding the canonical archive\n   380\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
