erived-views/epic.md:365:- **TC-5.4a: Archive remains after derived view creation**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:366:  - Given: A derived view has been created or refreshed\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:377:  - Given: A derived view cannot fully resolve source turns or metadata\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:423:Archive and derived views must remain usable across reloads, process pauses,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:430:5. System preserves the readable archive and returns bounded degraded states\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:441:  - Given: A derived view exists for a process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:443:  - Then: The derived view remains readable or can be rebuilt from turns\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:452:**AC-7.3:** Archive reads remain bounded for long processes.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:454:- **TC-7.3a: Archive read returns bounded page**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:457:  - Then: The platform returns a bounded page and indicates whether more entries are available\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:481:| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/archive/derived-views/refresh` | Requests rebuild or refresh of derived views from canonical turns |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:510:| page.cursor | string | no | non-empty when present | Cursor used to fetch this page |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:534:| page.cursor | string | no | non-empty when present | Cursor used to fetch this page |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:544:| viewKind | enum | yes | `turn_range` or `chunk_candidate` | Kind of structural derived view in this first slice |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:551:| viewStatus | enum | yes | `ready` or `degraded` | Whether the derived view resolved cleanly |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:552:| degradationReason | string | no | non-empty when present | Why the derived view degraded |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:600:- Archive reads return the first bounded page within 2 seconds for processes\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:602:- Turn reads return the first bounded page within 2 seconds under normal\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:622:- One degraded archive entry, turn, or derived view does not hide healthy\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:655:8. What pagination and indexing strategy keeps archive reads bounded for long\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:701:environment loss, with access controls and bounded degradation.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:729:- AC-5.1 (non-summarizing derived view over turn range)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:730:- AC-5.2 (derived view structural boundary)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:731:- AC-5.3 (derived view provenance)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:732:- AC-5.4 (derived view does not replace archive)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:737:**Delivers:** Archive entries and derived views show available artifact and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:755:- AC-7.3 (bounded archive reads)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:8:history while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:31:entries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:32:bounded degraded reads. It explicitly avoids model-generated summaries,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:41:| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:78:The design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derive