{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '660,678p'\"","aggregated_output":"   660\tthe artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\n   661\tstatus becomes `degraded` for the read response, or an enriched response\n   662\tincludes degraded related-context metadata without mutating the stored\n   663\tcanonical entry. Story 3 remains responsible for rendering that response\n   664\tstate to the user.\n   665\t\n   666\t### Flow 7: Return Later and Bound Long Reads\n   667\t\n   668\tThis flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\n   669\tviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\n   670\tpagination with default limits:\n   671\t\n   672\t- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n   673\t- turns: default 50, max 100\n   674\t- derived views: default 50\n   675\t\n   676\tA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\n   677\treturn degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\n   678\tavailable.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
