{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '668,676p'\"","aggregated_output":"   668\tThis flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\n   669\tviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\n   670\tpagination with default limits:\n   671\t\n   672\t- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n   673\t- turns: default 50, max 100\n   674\t- derived views: default 50\n   675\t\n   676\tA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2, 6, and 7 drift together on checkpoint-bound archive material: finalized runtime entries that need artifact/source linkage are withheld from the canonical archive until a later async checkpoint phase, so the archive can be incomplete immediately after execution completes.\",\"Stories 4, 5, and 7 are wired end-to-end, but the turn/view surfaces behave like rebuilders instead of cached bounded readers: every GET re-derives from the full archive, and derived views stop at the first 50 records with no way to read the remainder.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Tech-design Q7/Flow 6 says archive rows should store nullable related ids and stay readable even when related context is unavailable; the implementation instead defers some rows until checkpoint provenance resolves.\",\"Tech-design Q5/Q8 says cached turns and derived views exist to keep long reads bounded, but the current read path full-scans and rewrites caches on every request and omits derived-view pagination altogether.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Most Epic 7 behaviors are implemented and covered by passing automation: canonical archive taxonomy, idempotent append, authenticated archive/turn/view routes, provenance enrichment, degraded-entry rendering, and reload/reopen flows all have automated coverage.\",\"Coverage is weak around the completion-to-checkpoint window: the orchestrator tests explicitly poll for deferred archive rows to appear later, which means the suite does not prove immediate canonical visibility for all finalized entries.\",\"Long-process coverage proves a hard cap of 50 derived views, but it does not prove a contract for paging through the full derived-view set.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production createApp wiring uses the real Convex store, Local/Daytona provider registry, and Octokit checkpoint writer; the in-memory stores/adapters remain test seams rather than the live execution path.\",\"The material production-path gap is the async checkpoint bridge: some finalized archive rows are only appended after background checkpoint work finishes, so canonical archive completeness depends on a later phase instead of the completion boundary itself.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"epic7-deferred-archive-append-window\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Checkpoint-bound archive entries are not appended at finalization time\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` diverts any runtime archive entry with `artifactCheckpointIndex` or `sourceProvenanceBinding` into `deferredArchiveEntries` instead of appending it immediately (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:731-735,1789-1790`). In the normal production path, successful execution then schedules `runCheckpointAsync` and returns without appending those rows (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:644-662`). The actual append happens later inside checkpoint execution (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:1024-1031,1108-1115`). The orchestration test has to poll until `script:live-archive-1` eventually appears, proving the row is not immediately durable after completion (`tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts:731-749`). This leaves a crash/reload window where finalized material is missing from the canonical archive.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4b\",\"AC-3.2a\",\"AC-3.2b\",\"AC-7.1a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"epic7-bounded-read-contract-drift\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads do not implement the bounded cached-read contract\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` always calls `rebuildTurns` before serving any page (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:81-98`), and `rebuildTurns` always full-scans the archive via `listAllArchiveEntries` before rewriting the entire turn cache (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:54-69,102-124`). `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` likewise rebuilds turns and rewrites derived views on every GET (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:61-74`). After rebuilding, the service hard-slices the derived-view set to 50 (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:25,66,210-211`), while the shared contract and route schema expose no cursor or page metadata for derived views (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts:282-289`,`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts:37-46`). The client can only report how many structural views it got, with no affordance to fetch omitted results (`apps/platform/client/features/processes/derived-archive-views-section.ts:46-49`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/derived-archive-views-section.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"TD-Q5\",\"TD-Q8\",\"AC-7.1b\",\"AC-7.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The first `corepack pnpm run green-verify` run failed once in `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:1397`, but a full rerun of `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed. I could not determine whether that was a timing flake or a one-off environment hiccup.\",\"I did not execute the manual live-service checklist with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev`; conclusions are based on code review plus automated gate runs.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
