{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_115","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-7 are wired end to end through shared archive contracts, Convex archive tables, Fastify archive routes, execution finalization hooks, and the client archive/turn/derived-view surfaces.\",\"Archive-entry degradation now propagates consistently into turn and derived-view rebuilds via shared enrichment, so detached or missing provenance no longer degrades only the archive page.\",\"Long-history behavior diverges across surfaces: archive entries and turns expose bounded paging, but derived views truncate after 50 items with no continuation signal.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The canonical separation is intact: live websocket/current-object history remains on the process work surface, while finalized archive writes flow through `ArchiveFinalizationService` into `archiveEntries`.\",\"Derived-view reads drift from the tech design's cursor-bounded read contract. The design calls for cursor pagination with a default derived-view limit, but the current API exposes no paging inputs and silently slices the computed set.\",\"The default production execution stack uses real Local and Daytona adapters, but the script layer is still one shared runtime-audit payload rather than process-type-specific execution logic.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Both requested gates passed: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all`.\",\"Automated happy-path coverage is strong across Convex, server, client, and integration tests for archive persistence, finalization, read/reopen, turn derivation, derived views, and provenance degradation.\",\"Gate coverage still has explicit gaps: `guard:no-test-changes` and `test:e2e` are scaffold-only `SKIP` scripts, so there is still no executable browser/runtime end-to-end archive scenario enforced by automation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake provider adapter is wired into the default production registry: `DefaultProviderAdapterRegistry` resolves real Local and Daytona adapters, while `SingleAdapterRegistry` and `InMemoryProviderAdapter` stay test-only.\",\"The remaining non-real execution-path concern is the shared `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload` path, which generates a generic workspace-inspection run for every execution instead of process-type-specific runtime logic.\",\"No fake archive store or shim route was found in the archive read/write path itself; archive persistence still flows through Fastify services and `PlatformStore` into Convex.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derived archive views are hard-capped at 50 with no pagination contract\",\"evidence\":\"Flow 7 says archive entries, turns, and derived views use cursor pagination with default limits, including derived views at a default of 50 (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:668-674`). The derived-view route exposes no paging query (`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts:37-44`), the shared response has no page metadata (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts:282-285`), and the service simply `slice(0, 50)`s computed views (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:210-211`). Once a process has more than 33 turns, some `turn_range`/`chunk_candidate` views become unreachable with no `hasMore` signal.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Production execution still runs through one shared runtime-audit payload\",\"evidence\":\"`createApp` constructs `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`). `ScriptExecutionService` then always builds `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload(...)` unless a custom factory is injected (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:298-356`). That payload emits a generic workspace-inspection run with fixed archive/tool/model/process shapes (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:18-295`). This is not a fake provider path, but it is still a generic execution path rather than process-type-specific runtime logic.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter-registry.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Story and epic gate commands still include scaffold-only checks\",\"evidence\":\"`guard:no-test-changes` only prints `SKIP: guard:no-test-changes not implemented for this repo yet` and `test:e2e` only prints `SKIP: test:e2e scaffolded in Story 0; no executable suite yet` (`package.json:23-27`). `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed, but those gate legs are not yet enforcing the intended protections.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether the shared runtime-audit payload is an accepted interim production path or should be replaced before archive contents are treated as fully domain-real.\",\"Decide whether derived-view reads should implement the cursor pagination promised in the tech design, or whether the spec should explicitly bless a hard 50-view cap.\",\"Replace the scaffolded `guard:no-test-changes` and `test:e2e` scripts if those protections are required for future epic gates.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
